  "An OpenAI team built an internal beta product over five months with zero manually written code, estimating about 1/10th the time of hand-writing; it reached roughly a million lines of code and about 1,500 merged PRs, averaging 3.5 PRs per engineer per day with three engineers.": 1,
  "An OpenAI team built and shipped an internal beta product with 0 lines of manually written code over five months, starting from an empty repository in late August 2025; they estimate it took about 1/10th the time of writing by hand.": 1,
  "In OpenAI's harness engineering write-up, engineers drive PRs by instructing Codex to review its own changes locally, request further agent reviews locally and in the cloud, respond to feedback, and iterate until all agent reviewers are satisfied (a 'Ralph Wiggum Loop').": 1,
  "In the OpenAI experiment, throughput per engineer increased as the team grew from three to seven engineers.": 1,
  "OpenAI's harness-engineering report describes roughly 1,500 merged PRs over five months with initially three engineers, where agent review loops are used and human PR review is optional; these are throughput figures, not defect-detection measurements.": 1,
  "OpenAI's team had Codex review its own changes locally, request additional agent reviews locally and in the cloud, respond to feedback, and iterate until all agent reviewers were satisfied; humans may review PRs but are not required to, with almost all review effort pushed agent-to-agent.": 1,
  "OpenAI's team reported early progress was slower than expected because the environment was underspecified, and that their bottleneck became human QA capacity as code throughput increased.": 1,
  "The OpenAI harness-engineering experiment produced roughly a million lines of code and about 1,500 merged pull requests from three engineers initially, averaging 3.5 PRs per engineer per day.": 1,
